From a0eea77886282e29f0c939a34f22a7b15cd2242b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 22:48:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Speed up search without dropping multilingual or prefix recall

Draft implementation of:
- stamped ScanCount with touched string IDs
- sparse, byte-budgeted n-gram cache entries
- prepared candidate tokenization and exact-prefix SIFT4 shortcut
- mmap-backed multilingual place-prefix FST
- mmap-backed multilingual admin-alias FST

The FST paths are additive: the existing fuzzy bigram/SIFT4 path remains the
fallback and is not replaced. Compiled indexes must be regenerated because the
rkyv CypressMemDb schema gains new fields.
